            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to run out, then the Bengali for to start (an engine)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: বিগড়ানো",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বিগড়ানো — bigṛāno — \"to break down; to go wrong\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পথে আমাদের গাড়িটা বিগড়ে গেল। pôthe āmāder gāṛiṭā bigṛe gelô. Our car broke down on the way."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): সেই গাড়ি বিগড়ে গেল, sei gāṛi bigṛe gelô."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mostly in the -এ form with যাওয়া: বিগড়ে যাওয়া, of a machine, and of a mood."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বিগড়ানো (bigṛāno) is inherited: CDIAL lists Bengali bigṛā, \"to go bad\", under Sanskrit vighaṭatē, \"flies apart, is marred\" (CDIAL 11673); the machine sense is the modern use."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
